    "result_text": "The full suite is green. There's only one runnable test class (`AcceptanceTest`); the other files are the base/helper. **BUILD SUCCESS** with all tests passing.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `initials` field so the owner API returns the upper-cased first letters of `firstName` and `lastName`, dot-separated with a trailing dot (e.g. `J.S.`).\n\nTwo changes, following the existing `displayName` pattern:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `initials` string property to the `Owner` schema (the DTOs are generated from this spec at build time), so `OwnerDto` now carries the field and it's serialized in the `GET /api/owners/{id}` response.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression on `toOwnerDto` computing `initials` as `upper(firstName[0]) + \".\" + upper(lastName[0]) + \".\"`.\n\n`firstName`/`lastName` are `@NotEmpty` (validated non-empty at create), so `charAt(0)` is safe on persisted owners. The new `coreComputesInitials` acceptance test (`john`/`smith` \u2192 `J.S.`) passes, and the full build is green.",
